<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Jan-Apr energy demand up 1.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Jan-Apr energy demand up 1.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's energy demand edged up 1.9 percent to 59.07 million tonnes of oil equivalent (TOE) in the first four months of 1997 from 57.95 million a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Demand grew 11.8 percent in the first four months of 1996, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>Energy consumption growth slowed due to an industrial downturn, a rise in energy prices and warmer weather conditions, it said.</p>
<p>The breakdown of South Korea's demand for energy resources in the first four months, compared with the same period last year. (Figures in brackets are year-on-year growth in percentage):  </p>
<p>	  Jan-Apr 1997	  Jan-Apr 1996</p>
<p>	    Amount		  AmountTotal</p>
<p>	   59,067   (1.9)	57,953  (11.8)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p> Petroleum products    263,284  (-0.4)     264,247   (8.8)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 barrels)</p>
<p> LNG			   4,686  (33.9)	 3,499  (30.3)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Hard coal		   1,214 (-19.8)	 1,513 (-18.9)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
